# Finalise

When the user says `finalise`, `/finalise`, `fap`, `/fap`, `finalise-full`, `/ffap`, or `finalise and push`, run the matching npm script. Do not invent a manual test-commit-push handoff.

| User says | Command | Commit | Push |
|-----------|---------|--------|------|
| finalise / `/finalise` | `npm run finalise` | yes | no |
| fap / `/fap` / finalise and push | `npm run finalise:push` | yes | yes |
| finalise-full / `/finalise-full` | `npm run finalise:full` | yes | no |
| ffap / `/ffap` | `npm run finalise:full:push` | yes | yes |

- Contract: `iommarket-finalise-v1` in `scripts/finalise/trusted-actions.ts`
- Ordinary verify: `typecheck` + `test:run`
- Full verify: also `lint` + `build`
- Never apply Prisma/Supabase migrations or run `db:push` / `db:migrate` as part of finalise
- Repair only allowlisted failed steps with `npm run finalise:repair`, then rerun the original command once
- Never generically repair commit, push, database, or unknown steps
- State the branch and a short summary before any push
- Push changes to `staging` first. Direct pushes targeting `main` are rejected by finalise and the installed pre-push hook.
- Production changes go through an approved `staging` to `main` pull request. Never bypass the safeguards as a routine shortcut.

## Reuse successful tests

- Do not rerun a successful full test suite solely for finalise closure after repair. The registered scripts automatically reuse a local success receipt for identical inputs for up to 24 hours.
- Reuse requires matching tracked and nonignored untracked file contents, root environment files, dependency lockfiles, runtime and relevant environment. Failed, interrupted, stale, malformed or changed-input runs require fresh tests. No receipt is created if inputs change during the run.
- Typecheck, lint and build retain their existing gates. Never fabricate a receipt or manually bypass checks. Set `FINALISE_FORCE_TESTS=1` to explicitly request a fresh suite when investigating nondeterminism.
